{"title":"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/2/642a3134837deae29f73ef1e2df3daa87321b4e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1+x^3)\\left(1+2x^{3^2}\\right)\\cdots \\left(1+kx^{3^k}\\right) \\cdots \\left(1+1997x^{3^{1997}}\\right) = 1+a_1 x^{k_1} + a_2 x^{k_2} + \\cdots + a_m x^{k_m}\\]\" width=\"659\" height=\"32\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c722bdd55a0cb1c177c8bf7269d47b62cd94da1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i \\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/b/1eb239ac02729483468bf9d79708b9b1db6d21f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_1 &lt; k_2 &lt; \\cdots &lt; k_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"15\" />. Determine the remainder obtained when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/c/01cf8f4cf8d0916ff1f466f213c12473453a36d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We begin by determining the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd5a62655475da075af22c4d9f82f547b7b3f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" />. Experimenting, we find the first few <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/1454aaa4a0c2598b6347e956e2602b4a48008a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />s:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec25b2f4e8bcb96d11cc80eca12a5141e930f954.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k_{1} = 3, k_{2} = {3^2}, k_{3} = {3^2}+3, k_{4} = {3^3}...\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We observe that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b4452c4d936f4214092cfa6bd6cd1319f31739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${3^k}&gt;\\sum_{n=1}^{k-1} {3^n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"87\" height=\"51\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/1454aaa4a0c2598b6347e956e2602b4a48008a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> will be determined by the base 2 expansion of i. Specifically, every 1 in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a1796646819597a138efa6e6fb4c2c8b6df2d9a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{(n-1)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />s digit of the expansion corresponds to adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/c/59c404d8a8901ace9c02b39cb10d8dd226134c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/1454aaa4a0c2598b6347e956e2602b4a48008a81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/d/6ad471dcbee88e7845c37d8ea2ffebfff42fc257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1997 = 11111001101$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"159\" height=\"13\" /> base 2, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/2/ef2776c115da46de44ccbfb1bfced24494f29fab.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k_{1997}={3^{11}}+{3^{10}}+{3^9}+{3^8}+{3^7}+{3^4}+{3^3}+{3^1}.\\]\" width=\"364\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Now we look for ways to attain an element with degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd5a62655475da075af22c4d9f82f547b7b3f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" />. Since each sum of powers of 3 is unique, there is only one; namely, take the x element for every binomial with a degree of one of the added powers of 3 in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd5a62655475da075af22c4d9f82f547b7b3f5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_{1997}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" />, and the 1 for all else. Finally, since the coefficients of the x elements are equal to the degree to which the 3 is raised, we conclude\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/3/ab37335ef9fe448f53162f9af01d13f775950ff0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{1997}=11*10*9*8*7*4*3*1 =665\\boxed{280}.\\]\" width=\"365\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>-MRGORILLA\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005\">Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems\">Problems</a></b>, <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=14769\">Source</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 10 (page does not exist)\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mock_AIME_2_Pre_2005_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Mock AIME 2 Pre 2005 Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018040145\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.024 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.039 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 160/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1424/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 182/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3429/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.898      1 Template:Mock_AIME_box\n100.00%    7.898      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20273:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018040145 and revision id 141238. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}